From 59de0bf78b7cbcb4994add01601571e5269c2bfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:17:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 46/54] mac-bridge-app: native macOS QMX Bridge app with a
 virtual USB serial port

QMX Bridge.app (Swift/SwiftUI) replaces the Python mac-serial-bridge in one
window: Discover (QMXR? on UDP 7355), Probe (read-only ID; FA; MD; on port 3
and the I/Q copy's hello), the port-3 serial bridge and the TCI server for
WS / WSJT-X 3 / JTDX (USB demodulator, one-tone transmit as TA<Hz>;).

The serial port is either QMXSerialDriver.dext - a DriverKit IOUserSerial
driver that makes /dev/cu.QMX-NAS appear like a USB serial adapter - or a
pseudo-terminal linked at ~/cu.QMX-NAS (QMX Bridge Lite.app, no driver).
build.sh generates the Xcode project with XcodeGen and builds both apps;
README.md covers signing, approving the driver and the entitlement request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
